## 2. Core Escrow Lifecycle

| Method | Path | Auth | File |
|--------|------|------|------|
| POST | `/escrow` | 🔐 | server/app.py |
| GET | `/escrows` | | server/app.py |
| GET | `/escrow/{service_hash}` | | server/app.py |
| GET | `/escrow/{service_hash}/history` | | server/app.py |
| POST | `/release` | 🔐 | server/app.py |
| POST | `/refund` | 🔐 | server/app.py |
| POST | `/dispute` | 🔐 | server/app.py |
| POST | `/resolve` | 🔐 | server/app.py |
| GET | `/estimate` | | server/app.py |
| POST | `/compute-hash` | | server/app.py |

```bash
# Create escrow (payment header omitted for brevity — SDK signs it)
curl -s -X POST $BASE/escrow \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -H 'X-Payment: x402-v1;...;<signature>' \
  -d '{"service_hash":"<hex>","amount":5000,"receiver":"account-hash-<hex>"}' | jq

curl -s "$BASE/escrows?limit=20&status=active" | jq
curl -s $BASE/escrow/<service_hash> | jq
curl -s $BASE/escrow/<service_hash>/history | jq
curl -s "$BASE/estimate?amount=5000" | jq
curl -s -X POST $BASE/compute-hash \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"sender":"...","receiver":"...","amount":5000,"nonce":"abc"}' | jq

# Lifecycle (signed)
curl -s -X POST $BASE/release  -H 'X-Payment: ...' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"service_hash":"..."}' | jq
curl -s -X POST $BASE/refund   -H 'X-Payment: ...' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"service_hash":"..."}' | jq
curl -s -X POST $BASE/dispute  -H 'X-Payment: ...' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"service_hash":"...","reason":"non-delivery"}' | jq
curl -s -X POST $BASE/resolve  -H 'X-Payment: ...' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"service_hash":"...","verdict":"release","arbiter_sigs":[...]}' | jq
```

